Here are some generic beginner's hints.  Some of them are not totally
true and proper if you're trying to ascend, but they help to learn
the game.  I've left all the disclaimers out to save space.

Lots of little spoilers follow, of course.  Purists beware. 


1. Classes:
   Barbarians fight pretty well and start with intrinsic poison 
   resistence.  If you're still at the stage where you starve a 
   lot, they're a good class.
   Priests can tell whether items are cursed.  This saves a lot
   of grief.
   Valkyries start with a +3 shield, for an easy path to a decent
   AC.  And, with a bit of divine help and some gauntlets of 
   power, they can throw Mjollnir and get it back, which makes
   killing things pretty simple and safe.

2. Items:
   Ignore gems.  They're a waste of time unless you can identify 
   them.  You have better uses for those scrolls.
   Ignore spellbooks until you have a few levels under your belt.
   Assuming you're playing a "stupid" class, you'll do yourself
   more harm than good.
   Pets won't willingly step on cursed items.
   Drop everything on any altar and you'll know its curse status.
   Train your pet to rob stores using tripe.  One square directly
   inside the door is the legal shoplifting zone.  So stand in 
   the doorway, and when your pet drops something in the LSZ,
   throw tripe at your pet immediately.  Then pick up everything
   it brings you and sell the junk back.  Repeat until bored.   
   Scrolls of identify are your best friends.  If you get a bunch
   of them, it's worth a bit of holy water to bless them. 
   When not in a shop, engrave with your unknown wands to possibly
   identify them.
   Get a unicorn horn before you identify unknown potions by 
   drinking them.
   If you must identify scrolls and potions the hard way, follow
   some safety rules.  Get a unicorn horn to zap away blindness 
   and hallucination.  Take off your armor to avoid having it
   destroyed.  Drop your other scrolls and spellbooks to avoid
   losing it all to a scroll of fire.  And at least verify that
   things are uncursed first.
   Learn all the little messages you get when you use certain 
   items, so you can Name them the right thing.  
   Don't carry too much.  Wimpy monsters become lethal when they
   get multiple moves to your one.   
   Things you want:
   blessed bag of holding
   blessed luckstone
   blessed unicorn horn  
   boots of speed
   shield of reflection
   helm of brilliance
   gauntlets of power 
   blessed magic marker
   gray dragon scale mail
   amulet of life saving
   If you're lucky enough to get an early wish, remember to preface
   your favorite item with "blessed rustproof +3" (or +2 if you're
   wimpy), leaving out the parts that don't apply to your item. 

3. Religion: 
   Don't annoy your god.  Don't be a cannibal or abuse your pet
   or sacrifice humans (if not chaotic).
   Pray if you need to.  But not too often.  And pray after 
   dropping water on your altar to create holy water.  
   Once you find a free altar (no enemy priest), convert it
   by offering and then just keep on sacrificing until you 
   get really bored.  Lots of luck and artifacts come this way.

4. Food:
   Eat things right after you kill them.
   Remember which corpses give which intrinsics.  Remember which
   intrinsics you have and which you need.  Learn what all the
   little messages you get when you gain an intrinsic mean.
   Answer 'y' to "Stop eating?" prompts.
   Don't eat zombies and mummies.  Eat wraiths, though.
   Don't eat poisonous things until you have poison resistance.
   Except for the ones that might give you poison resistance. 
   Hint: killer bees.
   Save tripe for pet acqusition and training.
   
5. General path:
   Kill.  Eat.  Repeat.  What, too general?  :-> 
   Descend fairly quickly.  Explore everything, but don't sit 
   around.  Unless you have an altar, or a shop to rob, or 
   some such compelling reason, and sufficient food.
   The dwarvish mines will give you lots of corpses to eat, and
   some decent armor.  You can also get up to 7th level (speed)
   pretty quickly there.  If you're dying there, your AC is 
   probably bad and you're letting yourself get surrounded.  So 
   hang around the up-steps for awhile if you need to, and go 
   upstairs for breathers.  If you still keep dying in the Mines,
   I'd recommend a quick sortie into them to pick up some armor.
   Then a trip down to about level 10 of the Dungeons of Doom, 
   hopefully picking up nice stuff and maybe an altar.  Then
   the Mines should be simple. 
   There's always an altar on the town level of the Gnomish Mines.
   But I wouldn't try to convert it unless you're sure.  It'll 
   identify stuff's curse status either way.  
   There's always a luckstone in a secret room on the bottom 
   level of the Mines.  Bless it. 

Once again, these tips are pretty general, and they are sometimes 
the wrong way to go for long-term success.  But with a little practice,
you can clean out the Mines and make it down to about level 15 pretty 
easily.  Then you've made it to the next phase of the game.  Which is
easier, BTW. 

